 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "In mathlib/Mathlib/Analysis/MellinTransform.lean, line 45 (`MellinConvergent`) uses `(t : \u2102) ^ (s - 1) \u2022 f t` and line 91 (`mellin`) uses `\u222b t in Ioi 0, (t : \u2102) ^ (s - 1) \u2022 f t`. Setting `s' - 1 = -(s + 1)` gives `s' = -s`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/MellinTransform/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Reword to \"Absolute convergence of the upper tail `\u222b_{a}^\u221e y ^ (-(s + 1)) \u2022 f y` (the Mellin tail at `-s`) is integrability of `y ^ (-(s.re + 1)) * \u2016f y\u2016`.\"",
   "issue": "The docstring says \"Absolute convergence of an upper Mellin tail at `s`\", but the integrand `(y : \u2102) ^ (-(s + 1)) \u2022 f y` is the Mellin kernel at `-s`. Under Mathlib's convention the kernel at `s` is `t ^ (s - 1)`, so a reader would apply the lemma at the wrong argument.",
   "line": 330
  }
 ],
